  "about": {
    "heading": "Elara Voss",
    "teaser": "Berlin-based photographer working in portraiture and landscape. Fifteen years of looking for the minute before and the minute after, when a subject reveals something unguarded. Published in Foam Magazine, The British Journal of Photography and Le Monde.",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Born in Hamburg, currently based in Berlin. Elara began making photographs at seventeen with a borrowed Rolleiflex, drawn to the way medium format film compressed time into a single held breath.",
      "Over fifteen years she has developed a body of work that refuses the decisive moment in favor of something quieter — the minute before and the minute after, when a subject is most themselves.",
      "Her work has appeared in Foam Magazine, The British Journal of Photography, Aperture Online, and Le Monde M. She has exhibited at Foam Amsterdam, C/O Berlin, and Rencontres d'Arles."
    ],
